\label{definition-representable-morphism}
A morphism $f : x \to y$ of a category $\mathcal{C}$ is said to be
{\it representable} if for every morphism $z \to y$
in $\mathcal{C}$ the fibre product $x \times_y z$ exists.
\end{definition}

